const MAX_TIMEOUT = 30000; // Default timeout of 30 seconds

class CodeMirrorLintService {
    private $rest;
    private $currentRequest;

    public function __construct(RestClient $rest) {
        $this->rest = $rest;
    }

    public async function lint(WikitextDocument $doc): bool {
        if ($this->currentRequest !== null) {
            $this->currentRequest->abort();
        }

        try {
            $response = await $this->rest->post('/v1/transform/wikitext/to/lint', [
                'wikitext' => $doc->toString(),
                'timeout' => MAX_TIMEOUT,
            ]);

            $errors = $response->getData();
            // Process errors as needed
            return true;
        } catch (RestException $e) {
            mw.log.warn('[CodeMirror] Lint request failed: ' . $e->getMessage());
            return false;
        }
    }
}
```

This revised code includes a timeout setting and aborts any previous requests before making a new one. It also uses a try-catch block to handle potential errors and logs warnings appropriately.

